# Wireframe: App Shell

## Purpose & Flow Context

Shared application frame present on all authenticated screens. Provides primary navigation (sidebar), user menu (header), and notification indicator. Entry: after login. Exit: logout redirects to login. All screens inherit this shell.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `⚠` | Warning / due date | `📎N` | N attachments |
| `💬N` | N comments | `🔗` | Card relationship |
| `👤` | User / mention | `○ ●` | Radio unselected / selected |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

All screens inherit these.

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `main`, `aside`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | One `h1` per screen, `h2` for sections |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space, Escape, Arrow keys |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, never color alone |

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: 12-column layout. Spacing cadence: 4px rhythm.

**App-shell**: Regions:

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Sidebar | Logo, nav items, project list, cycles, user info | Collapsible to icon-only (56px / 240px) |
| Header | Breadcrumb, search, notification badge, user avatar dropdown | Sticky top |
| Main content | Route-driven content area | Fills remaining space, scrollable |

**Content hierarchy**:
1. Sidebar navigation — primary wayfinding
2. Header — secondary actions, notifications
3. Main content — active view

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  +--------+  +-------------------------------------------------+  |
|  | SIDEBAR |  | HEADER                                         |  |
|  |         |  | [Breadcrumb]        [Search] [🔔3] [👤▼]      |  |
|  | [Logo]  |  +-------------------------------------------------+  |
|  | ---     |  |                                                    |
|  | [Issues]|  |  MAIN CONTENT                                      |
|  | [Board] |  |  (route-driven, scrollable)                        |
|  | ---     |  |                                                    |
|  | Projects|  |                                                    |
|  | > MyApp |  |                                                    |
|  | ---     |  |                                                    |
|  | [👤JL]  |  |                                                    |
|  +--------+  +-------------------------------------------------+  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Sidebar toggle | Sidebar (collapsible) | Click collapses/expands sidebar | Persisted to localStorage |
| Nav items | Sidebar nav-item | Click routes to view; active state highlighted | Long labels truncate with ellipsis |
| Notification badge | NotificationBadge | Shows unread count from WebSocket store | 0 = hidden; 99+ overflow |
| User avatar | DropdownMenu (trigger = avatar) | Click opens user menu (profile, settings, logout) | — |
| Search toggle | Button (icon) | Click opens search overlay | — |

## Data Display

N/A — app shell is structural, not data-display.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Logo | Application identity | Brand name or logomark |
| "Issues" nav | Primary entity navigation | Consistent across all views |
| "Board" nav | Kanban board view | — |
| Notification count | Unread activity indicator | Shows number, not dot |

## States

### Populated (Default)

The layout shown above — sidebar expanded, header visible, content area populated by route.

### Empty

N/A — shell is always present.

### Loading

Skeleton sidebar + header render immediately. Content area shows route-level loading skeleton.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  +========+  +=================================================+  |
|  | SKEL   |  | HEADER (static)                                 |  |
|  | [====] |  +=================================================+  |
|  | [====] |  |  CONTENT SKELETON (route-dependent)               |
|  | [====] |  |  [====] [====] [====]                             |
|  |        |  |  [====] [====] [====]                             |
|  +========+  +=================================================+  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Error

N/A — shell is structural; errors appear in content area.

### Success / Confirmation

N/A — no state-changing action on shell itself.

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Sidebar full (240px), header full |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Sidebar collapses to icon-only by default; toggleable |
| Mobile (<768px) | Sidebar → off-canvas overlay; header compacts (search icon-only) |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | `header` (Header), `nav` (Sidebar), `main` (Main content) |
| Heading order | Sidebar sections h2, content h1 (route-driven) |
| Reading / Focus order | Sidebar → Header → Main content |
| Accessible names | Sidebar toggle: `aria-label="Toggle sidebar"`; User menu: `aria-label="User menu"`; Notification badge: `aria-label="3 unread notifications"` |
| Keyboard operability | Tab through sidebar items, Enter to navigate; Escape closes off-canvas sidebar on mobile |
| Target size | All nav items ≥24×24 CSS px; sidebar toggle ≥24×24 CSS px |
| Focus not obscured | Sticky header does not overlap focused sidebar items |
| Non-color intent | Active nav item uses icon + bold text, not color alone |

*Defer to design-system: pixel contrast, focus-appearance, per-component target-size/keyboard.

---

## Assumptions & Open Questions

### Base UI Primitives (shadcn/ui)

These components are referenced in wireframes as design-system components but are not defined in the current DS catalog (`design-system.md`). They are standard shadcn/ui primitives — part of the project's declared stack (`docs/stack-frontend.md`: shadcn/ui + `@radix-ui/*`). Their anatomy, states, and a11y contract follow shadcn/ui conventions and will be documented in a future DS pass.

| Component | Referenced In | shadcn/ui Source |
|-----------|---------------|------------------|
| Avatar | App Shell (user avatar), Issue Detail, Issue List | `@radix-ui/react-avatar` |
| Badge | Issue List (status), Issue Detail (status, labels) | `@radix-ui/react-badge` or custom |
| Button | All screens (icon, link, primary, secondary variants) | `@radix-ui/react-slot` |
| Input | Issue List (search), Login (email/password), Issue Form (title) | `@radix-ui/react-slot` |
| Textarea | Issue Form (description), Issue Detail (comment input) | Standard `<textarea>` |
| List | Issue Detail (comments, metadata) | Standard `<ul>`/`<li>` |
| Link | Issue Detail (back), Login (sign up) | `@radix-ui/react-slot` |
| Icon | Issue List (priority, attachment, comment icons), EmptyState, ErrorBanner | `lucide-react` |

**Status**: Deferred — these are included in the project's existing shadcn/ui + lucide-react dependencies. A future DS pass will add full entries for project-specific variants (e.g., `StatusBadge` with colour mapping to issue workflow states).

### Locale

**Assumption**: Single-locale (English). No i18n or RTL accommodations in the current wireframe pass. If multi-locale is required, every text slot flagged with microcopy intent will need i18n key wiring and text-expansion allowance.

